reviewer_concerns.value:
The authors provided extensive additional evaluations that addressed most of the concerns from reviewer gTmW; 

Reviewer t7hd raised questions about the types of uncertainty in dynamics considered by the submission, the proposed benchmark being limited and "hand-crafted", and real-world planning scenarios (that requires continuous dynamics), these concerns were acknowledged by the authors as limitations or future work;

Reviewer WjYP had concerns on limited novelty, missing baselines, and some clarification questions. These have been mostly addressed by the rebuttal ("novelty" is often subjective, but the authors clarified that a main distinction is that the proposed framework actively seeks information);

Reviewer TXuA shared a similar concern on the simplicity of the framework, and crucially its performance on more complex and dynamic real-world environments. The authors attempted to mitigate the concern via the diversity (as opposed to the complexity) of the benchmark, which unfortunately doesn't address the concern properly.
